Lets entries re-admitted from the deferred set (an unfreeze, a superseded
entry, a re-classified want) and approve's entries skip quarantine matching
and the brake again, as before 3cba684 (§8.1, §8.2): admit() no longer joins
a candidate whose version is quarantined, or dominates a quarantined one, to
that held item, and every group passes without the brake being evaluated.
The rest of admit() stays: a version already wanted still only names a
source, and 20a7504's rule that an entry of a batch still held joins it. No
seed fails with this patch (0 to 9,999, and 0 to 499 at 2,000 steps): a
re-admitted entry keeps its own accepted batch's id, so I5 never matches it,
and no other invariant sees it. The patch names the rule's unit tests:
3cba684's own and the one that replaced this pin's seed.

